preConditionHook:
// First target after fading a countertrend bar: the signal bar's own far
// extreme. The prior bar is read UNCONDITIONALLY -- EasyLanguage does not
// short-circuit (EL_LogicalEval_Probe) and Max Bars Back has to cover the
// subscript on every bar anyway -- and only the freeze is conditional.
// BarsSinceEntry() is 0 on the bar the entry FILLS and 0 while flat, never a
// -1 sentinel (EL_FEATURES `barssinceentry`, VERIFIED), so on the fill bar
// bar [1] is the SIGNAL bar the trade was entered from, and the capture simply
// re-arms on every flat bar. Holding the price rather than re-reading
// high[BarsSinceEntry + 1] keeps the deepest subscript at 1 instead of the
// length of the longest trade.
// tolerancePoints is in PRICE UNITS: MinMove / PriceScale are UNKNOWN.
prevHigh = high[1];
prevLow = low[1];
if (el_eq((double)ctx.BarsSinceEntry(), 0.0)) {
    sigHigh = prevHigh;
    sigLow = prevLow;
}
